From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: implement VLAN-aware bridge domains

Add the low level helpers for the ingress VLAN pipeline, in preparation for
offloading VLAN-aware bridges: the per-port default C-VID, the per-port
ingress filtering mode (the forward command on a translation miss), and the
ingress VLAN translation rules and actions, which match packets by ingress
port bitmap and tag format, optionally keyed by VLAN ID, assign a VSI, and
optionally remove the C-tag for a routed ingress topology.

Extend the bridge offload to VLAN-aware bridges. Each VLAN of an offloaded
bridge is backed by its own VSI: ingress VLAN translation rules assign
tagged packets of the member ports and untagged packets of the PVID ports
to the VSI, and the per-VSI egress tag modes provide tagged or untagged
egress per port, with the CPU port always tagged so the software ports of
the bridge see the VLAN of flooded packets. The per-port default C-VID
supplies the VLAN ID when a packet received untagged on a PVID port leaves
through a tagged port.

Merged from:
  0505-01-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-vlan-config-helpers.patch
  0505-02-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-offload-vlan-aware-bridges.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

